  "limits": [
    "A completed received character starts native RXIDLE detection. RXIDLE is not the programmable TIMCR=3/TIMOV timer.",
    "TIMCR stays disabled; no configurable duration or numeric timeout is promised.",
    "Reading RDR does not clear RC; observed receive flags require separate R1W0 acknowledgement with the existing 0x1fff no-op seed.",
    "A received character while RC remains set can overwrite RDR and set ORE; per-byte task service is still required.",
    "ORE > PE > FE > NE is retained software policy, not vendor error arbitration.",
    "For co-latched RC and RXIDLE no source establishes the temporal side of the boundary; consuming observed RC before success is best effort.",
    "No continuous reception, background queue, ring buffer or bounded completion if neither full nor idle occurs.",
    "L011 uses the L010 UART register version but retains its own source, SYSCTRL and package authority.",
    "Existing package exclusions, oscillator reservations, ownership and L012 UART3 RCC inspection limits remain applicable."
  ],
